# /save — curate an inbox signal into an atomic note

## Usage
/save <inbox_path> [--type note|project|area|resource] [--title "..."] [--links "[[A]],[[B]]"]

## What this does
Routes a captured inbox signal to an atomic note under Brain/notes/:
1. Reads the inbox file
2. Routes to the correct path based on `.vault-meta/mode.json` methodology
3. Writes an atomic note (one idea per file) with wikilinks and valid frontmatter
4. Updates the domain `Brain/index/_index.md`
5. Appends the event to today's log

## Atomic note rules
- ONE idea per file — if the source has multiple ideas, split into multiple /save calls
- Include at least one wikilink `[[related-concept]]` connecting to existing notes
- Frontmatter must have: title, created, type, status: curated

## When to use
After /capture when you're ready to process the inbox signal into a permanent note.

## Instructions
1. Read the inbox file to understand the signal
2. Determine: is this atomic (one idea)? If not, split before saving.
3. Identify 1–3 related notes to wikilink (use /find to discover them)
4. Execute: `brain save <inbox_path> --title "<concise-title>" --links "<wikilinks>"`
5. Report the created note path
6. Optionally run the verifier before committing
